  "<b>Flashcards</b> asks you to recall and grade yourself. <b>Learn</b> offers four candidates and grades the click for you.": "<b>卡片</b>：自己回忆、自己评分。<b>选择</b>：给出四个选项，点击后自动评分。",
  "<b>One line</b> opens every reply with the phrasing a native speaker would have used. <b>Weave</b> also asks Claude to work your ten weakest words into the answer. Both spend a line of every response.": "<b>一行</b>：每个回复开头给出母语者的说法。<b>融入</b>：另外请 Claude 把你最薄弱的十个词编进回答里。两者都会占用每个回复的一行。",
  "A cap on unseen cards only. Reviews that are due are never held back — those are the ones that decay.": "只限制未见过的卡片。待复习的卡片从不被压后——它们才是会遗忘的。",
  "A card carries the pronunciation of its word in IPA. eSpeak NG writes it on this machine for nothing when it is installed; otherwise the builder writes it, at a few tokens a card.": "每张卡片都带有单词的国际音标。若本机装有 eSpeak NG，它会免费写出；否则由生成器写出，每张卡片花费几个 token。",
  "A chapter is the topic its cards share. Rename it and every card in it moves along.": "章节就是卡片共有的主题。重命名它，其中的所有卡片都会一起移动。",
  "A deck is a pair: the language you write in and the one you are learning. They can never be the same.": "卡组是一对语言：你书写的语言和你在学的语言。两者永远不能相同。",
